#: ../../Chords.rst:89
msgid "How do I make Chords?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:91
msgid ""
"You can make chords for your CharaChorder using a few different methods "
"which we will discuss below. In order to make a chord, you will have to "
"indicate your desired :ref:`chord input<Chords:Chord Input>` as well as "
"your desired :ref:`chord output<Chords:Chord Output>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:97
msgid ""
"Your CharaChorder device already comes with some chords loaded onto it. "
"These cover some of the most common words in the English language. You "
"can click on the link to see that list in an external tab: `Starter "
"Chords "
"<https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1G_A77DsyoM2hod3by2BzM7Wcj3JGJsmNw7dAz98wS3U/edit?usp=sharing>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:102
msgid ""
"You can create custom chords on the :doc:`Device Manager<Device "
"Manager>`. Additionally, you, can create chords on the go by using "
":ref:`impulse chording<Chords:Impulse Chording>`. Read on for specific "
"instructions on how to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:107
msgid "On Device Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:109
msgid ""
"The CharaChorder Device Manager is our official web based configuration "
"tool designed for CharaChorder devices. On there, you can do a variety of"
" things. You can read all about Device Manager in this "
":doc:`section<Device Manager>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:113
msgid ""
"The process for adding chords to your CharaChorder is the same on all of "
"our CharaChorder devices. You can :ref:`add new chords<Chords:Adding New "
"Chords on Device Manager>`, or :ref:`import an existing chord "
"library<Device Manager:Restoring from a Backup>`. Read how below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:120
msgid "Adding New Chords on Device Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:122
msgid ""
"The steps to do this are :ref:`in the Device Manager documentation<Device"
" Manager:Creating a Chord>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:125
msgid "Impulse chording"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:127
msgid ""
"Impulse chording is a method of adding chords that doesn’t require "
"anything except your CharaChorder after a space to type in. It allows you"
" to create ‘on the fly’, custom chords which can be spontaneously created"
" anywhere that you can type via the Impulse menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:132
msgid ""
"The idea of impulse chords is that whenever you come across a word that "
"you don’t have a chord for, you can instantly create one mid-email, mid-"
"discord chat, mid-whatever, without the need to switch windows, import, "
"connect, etc. Just punch in your input and output via the Impulse Menu "
"and then keep typing without skipping a beat. Read below for instructions"
" on how to create an impulse chord on your specific device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:140
msgid ""
"**Note:** When creating an impulse chord, all keystrokes are recorded as "
"part of the output. If you make a mistake when defining the chord output,"
" trigger escape and start over instead of deleting the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:145
msgid "Creating an Impulse Chord on the CharaChorder One"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:147
msgid ""
"Standard process for creating an impulse chord on a CharaChorder One: In "
"short: 1. CHORD INPUT, 2. CALL IMPULSE, 3. TYPE OUTPUT, 4. CONFIRM OUTPUT"
" 5. CONFIRM INPUT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:-1
msgid "Impulse chording on the CharaChorder One"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:156 ../../Chords.rst:185 ../../Chords.rst:214
msgid ""
"Anywhere that you can see a cursor, chord the input you want (example: "
"``b+u+r+s+t``). You will either see a jumble of letters (example: "
"“tsubr”) or you will see a chord which is already programmed to that "
"input. If you continue, any conflicts will be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:161
msgid "Call the impulse command the hard coded chord ``i+DUP``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:163 ../../Chords.rst:192 ../../Chords.rst:221
msgid ""
"Follow the prompt and type your output in character entry mode. (example:"
" >I<mpulse output: burst )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:165 ../../Chords.rst:194 ../../Chords.rst:223
msgid "Press enter to confirm your output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:166 ../../Chords.rst:195
msgid ""
"Verify that the desired input is correct (you will see a confirmation "
"message similar to this: >I<mpulse input: b + r + u + t + s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:168 ../../Chords.rst:197 ../../Chords.rst:227
msgid ""
"If the input is incorrect, perform your desired input at this step. Once "
"the input is the desired input, press enter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chords.rst:171 ../../Chords.rst:200
msgid "These steps should take 1-3 seconds."
msgstr ""

